{
  "dom_id": "step-q183350",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Find the missing entries in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| Whenever $A,$ then $B$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $B$ whenever $A$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $B,$ provided that $A$ | {{field-3}} |",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"Whenever $A,$ then $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$B$ whenever $A$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$B,$ provided that $A$\" means $A⇒B$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| Whenever $A,$ then $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $B$ whenever $A$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $B,$ provided that $A$ | $A⇒B$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
